cuems-engine (0.1.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Coordinated xml-refactor landing (cuems-utils feature 016): every CUEMS
    repository moves to its own next stable minor. The released 0.1.0rc2-3
    entry below is kept as it shipped.
  * Version sites agree on 0.1.1. This changelog said 0.1.0rc2-3 while
    pyproject.toml and cuemsengine.__version__ said 0.1.0rc7; the package
    and the module had never agreed.
  * Depends: cuems-utils (>= 0.1.1), cuems-utils (<< 0.1.2~); was
    (>= 0.1.0rc16), (<< 0.1.1~). cuems-common (>= 1.3.1~), was
    (>= 1.3.0-23~), which the released 1.3.0-23..-25 satisfied without the
    node_role vocabulary. cuems-engine-mock: cuems-engine (>= 0.1.1), was
    (>= 0.1.0rc2). pyproject: cuemsutils >=0.1.1,<0.1.2.
  * Depends: libmtcmaster (>= 0.0.2-0), new. The engine loads
    libmtcmaster.so.0 (src/cuemsengine/core/libmtc.py) and nothing declared
    it. 0.0.2-0 is the published release (GitHub v0.0.2-0), not bumped.
  * poetry.lock is NOT relocked: cuemsutils 0.1.1 is unresolvable until it is
    published. tests/test_lock_is_current.py (strict xfail) turns red the day
    the lock is regenerated, so the obligation cannot be forgotten.
  * Reconciled with debian/bookworm at 1c12959 (0.1.0rc6-6): this release
    absorbs 0.1.0rc6-2 .. 0.1.0rc6-6, and the released entries 0.1.0rc2-1
    .. 0.1.0rc6-6 below (with the 0.1.0rc5-2 .. rc5-6 hotfix builds) are kept
    as they shipped. What the absorbed builds changed:
    - 869f8hfra: video scale readback with float32 tolerance; placement
      failures logged at ERROR and recorded per cue; disarm skips layers
      removed by /reset. 869f8v8yv: the dead VideoPlayer class is gone.
    - 869f9wqpn: a node pre-arms its next segment; one arm in flight per
      cue; arm epochs (publish or abandon); the JACK port wait ends on a
      dead player; a GO that cannot arm its cue skips it and advances.
    - 869fat84r: a video cue takes its pixel size from the project; nodes
      report their own media files that differ.
    - 869fa89uh: a play-once video cue no longer wraps to frame 0.
    - 869fc8ytz: cross-node Auto follow relay (run_seq in every GO).
    - 869fbyjzx, 869fcvz85: an audio player is wired only once it reports
      RUNNING; edge-by-edge repair at GO.
    - 869fedahu: cue names on the :9190 channel.
    - 869evtdf7: orphan sweeps never abort a load.
    - 869dr2kzh, 869ebkkme: project_status with three states; node adoption
      from the UI; cluster_warning.
    - 869fgq3xv: unrouted video outputs stay dark.
    - 869fhjdq5, 869fhjdp8: the stop_project ActionCue; cue ADD/UPDATE
      ignored while not running; script_finished removed.
    - 869fh8kef: a project unload reaches the nodes as an unload.
    - Packaging: isolated build venv, rtmidi vendoring check; cffi-gen-src
      no longer shipped; mock wrappers renamed (Conflicts covers both
      players); SPDX headers.
  * ADAPTED to the 0.1.1 library while absorbing: node output lookups read
    the typed device mappings and take outputs only (35cbe78); mock audio
    players register their JACK ports and print the ready line (d50ee4b);
    ids of the absorbed code leave through id_str and enter through as_id.
  * CONDITION (stop_project): cuems-utils 0.1.1 must contain rc17's
    stop_project ActionType value, or a project with a stop_project cue
    cannot be loaded or saved. See
    specs/009-release-line-reconciliation/upstream-reports/cuems-utils-x1-x4.md.
  * UPGRADE EVERY HOST TOGETHER: the GO payload carries run_seq, which is
    not wire-compatible with engines before 0.1.0rc6-3, and an engine before
    0.1.0rc6-6 has no unload handler.

