cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-6) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm:
    - 869fh8kef (#41): a project unload reaches the nodes as an unload. The
      controller used to forward it as a STOP, and a node's STOP re-arms the
      project it still holds, so every node killed its players and started
      new ones for a project that was no longer loaded, and kept its
      script, load status and /tmp/cuems.show.lock. The controller now
      removes its show lock and forwards /engine/command/unload; the node
      tears the project down as a load does (now shared as
      _teardown_project: cue threads, DMX blackout, video layers, mixer,
      audio players, disarm), aborts in-flight arms, forgets the script,
      sets load="", removes the lock and arms nothing. Refused while
      running. Ends the run for the cross-node follow relay like STOP and
      load.
    - Docs: the A/V loop sync guarantee (README, CLAUDE.md).
  * No dependency change (cuems-utils >= 0.1.0rc17). The whole cluster must
    run this engine: an older node has no unload handler and keeps the
    project armed until the next load.

