cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-4) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm:
    - 869ebkkme, 869dr2kzh (#32): node adoption from the UI. The engine
      relays nodelist_modify to cuems-nodeconf, refusing at once when
      nodeconf is not running and while a project is running or loaded.
      /engine/status/cluster_warning tells the UI which project nodes are
      missing or unreachable at load; it warns and never blocks GO.
      project_status tells a stopped project from no project and returns
      its uuid; a failed load no longer leaves the previous project's name
      on the wire. Pairs with cuems-editor 0.1.0rc1-7.
    - 869fgq3xv (#33): a video cue aimed at an output the node does not
      drive (dropped at start: no region in display.conf, or
      enabled=false) is no longer loaded. It stays dark instead of being
      letterboxed across the working screens, keeps its place on the
      timeline (Auto follows, cross-node announces and loops are timed as
      if it played), and is logged as UNROUTED_VIDEO_OUTPUT at every load.
      The shared decoder moves to the first output that is driven.
      display.conf enabled= is read exactly as the videocomposer reads it.
      Behaviour change: such cues go from mis-placed to dark; grep the
      node journal for UNROUTED_VIDEO_OUTPUT after the first load. The
      engine reads display.conf only at start: after a hand edit, restart
      the videocomposer AND the node engine.

