cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm:
    - 869fa89uh (#23): a play-once video cue no longer wraps to frame 0 at
      its end; videocomposer wraparound is enabled only for cues that
      repeat.
    - 869fc8ytz (#25): an Auto follow into a cue on another node starts
      it; the controller relays the follow to the owning node. Every GO
      value is now a dict carrying run_seq: the WHOLE CLUSTER must run
      this engine (controller and every node).
    - 869fbyjzx, 869fcvz85 (#27): an audio player is wired to the mixer
      only once it reports RUNNING, so RtAudio's auto-connect to
      system:playback_* is always removed (no more doubled audio outside
      mixer volume); the GO-time check repairs the wiring edge by edge;
      arm-wait log lines say whether a GO waited or fell back.
    - 869fedahu (#28): the controller broadcasts each cue's name on the
      :9190 channel after every load (/engine/status/cue_name/<uuid>) and
      replays it to late clients. Additive; older UIs ignore it.
    - 869evtdf7 (#29): orphan sweeps never abort a project load. An
      orphaned player the node could not kill (EPERM) used to abort the
      load after the old project was torn down; both sweeps and the zombie
      JACK client cleanup now log and go on, match only own-user players
      by argv[0], and warn at start about unknown player binary names. A
      failing command callback is logged with its traceback.
    - #30: AudioMixer wait tests count only the test thread's sleeps
      (test-only).

