cuems-engine (0.1.0rc5-3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Supersedes 0.1.0rc5-2, which must not be deployed: its PreArm cleanup
    ran AFTER arm() had published the cue, so after a STOP -> GO -> GO
    inside one in-flight arm it could disarm a cue the restarted run was
    already playing, or leave it playing on a player the STOP had killed
    (869f9wqpn; found in the review of cuems-engine PR #22).
  * Publish or abandon: an arm belongs to the STOP/load epoch in which it
    was requested. The epoch moves in stop_all_cues() (the first step of a
    STOP and of a load) and in disarm_all(). An arm whose epoch moved is
    refused before it starts, or abandoned at the publish gate: the cue is
    never marked armed, and what the arm built is released by the arming
    thread itself. No background thread disarms after the fact any more.
  * One arm in flight per cue ID (not per object); a thread that waited on
    another thread's arm arms the cue itself if that arm was abandoned or
    failed, within the same 5 s wait.
  * go() no longer wipes a STOP that lands while it is re-arming a cue:
    the epoch check and the _stop_requested reset are one lock section
    (this line had no STOP barrier in go() at all). A cue dispatched
    before a STOP does not play after it.
  * disarm_all() clears the armed list together with its snapshot; clearing
    it after the loop could leave a cue loaded but unplayable until a
    reload.
  * The JACK port wait ends when the player PROCESS has exited (a STOP or a
    load killed it mid-wait) instead of running its full ~15 s. The wait
    for a live player is unchanged.
  * A GO whose cue cannot be armed in time skips it, advances the pointer
    in lockstep with the controller and logs one ERROR line naming the cue
    and why. It used to leave the node one GO behind until a STOP.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:40:28 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc5-2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Hotfix on 0.1.0rc5-1 (branch hotfix/rc5-2-prearm, based on 86b6290 =
    rc5-1 + the isolated build venv). Carries ONLY two fixes; it does NOT
    include 869ej4x38 (phase-2 dispatch reorder), 869f8hfra or anything
    else from rc_1 after rc5.
  * Backport of 869f79ecc (Badajoz first-run desync), 20 commits
    cherry-picked with -x from rc_1 (0509385..5fe9d6e): the controller
    ships the GO anchor inside GO and nodes resolve it (only from a live
    controller MTC); setnextcue's lookahead runs on a PreArm background
    thread off _command_lock; _arm_ahead skips other nodes' cues; the
    PreArm walk governs arm()'s recursion and pre-arms audio too; JACK
    port-registration time is logged. The anchor half needs the
    controller AND every node on this version.
  * NEW: a node pre-arms its next segment when a GO advances its pointer
    with nothing local to play (Medina sala1, 2026-09-30: ctrl go -> ctrl
    pause -> node go; the node's first cue fired 240 ms late on every
    run -- a shape 869f79ecc does not cover). The shared go-chain walk
    also stops the load pre-arm from giving up at a local-but-disabled
    cue. The segment's first cue and its lookahead are both armed on the
    PreArm background thread, never under _command_lock, so a STOP or the
    next GO is not held up by an audio player's spawn + JACK port wait.
    Whatever a PreArm thread armed (including arm()'s own recursion) is
    undone if a STOP or a load happened underneath it, so no cue is left
    marked armed with a player STOP just killed.

